<title>MOROCCO: Morocco's raises 425.5 mln dirhams at auction.</title>
<headline>Morocco's raises 425.5 mln dirhams at auction.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morocco's Treasury raised 425.5 million dirhams at its weekly treasury bill auction, Bank al-Maghrib (central bank) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Rates and amounts (in million dirhams) were accepted as follows:</p>
<p>    MATURITY	BID	   AMOUNT	INTEREST RATE</p>
<p>    13 weeks	10.5	    10.5	 7.00</p>
<p>    52 weeks	51.5	    51.5	 8.00</p>
<p>    Five years    33.5	    33.5	 9.00</p>
<p>    10 years     330	     330	   9.50</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    Total	   425.5	   425.5</p>
<p>The spokeswoman said the interest rate on 13-week treasury bills was cut by half a point to 7.00 percent after the treasury rejected commercial banks' offers at 7.50 and 7.25 percent since June 24.</p>
<p>Maturity date was set on July 28, 1997.</p>
<p>($1= 9.8 dirhams)</p>
<p>-- Newsroom +212-7 726518</p>
